  "lawGradeScale": "v4 law grading scale (native canon scale, strongest first): DERIVED, LOCKED, MAPPED, PARTIAL, SPLIT, OPEN, DEFINITIONAL. Mapping to C0-C6 unruled - tracked as OI-0011.",
  "statementTechnical": "General relativity. The proposed mapping: frame transformation <-> moral perspective transformation; the equivalence principle <-> grace has invariant content across moral frames; covariance <-> spiritual law holds in all moral reference frames. Canonical grade OPEN: gap named, no structural result yet. The moral-frame transformation set is unwritten - the monoid finding is a sketch; its axioms must be written down and checked (OI-0004). Disposition AM-1 pending David: restore as Law 9 or rule eight laws plus wrapper (OI-0003). Lean action: define what a moral frame transformation would need to be.",
  "statementPlain": "Relativity says every observer measures differently and something invariant holds underneath. The proposal: grace looks different from different moral frames but carries invariant content. This is the weakest law in the canon - graded OPEN at the source, with its core object (a moral-frame transformation group) not yet written down and its place in the ten awaiting a ruling. Nothing here is proven; the gap is named, which is what OPEN means.",
  "mathematicalForm": "No canonical form yet; required: a concrete transformation group for moral frames (unwritten - OI-0004)",
  "mathFormNormal": "No canonical form yet; required: a concrete transformation group for moral frames (unwritten - OI-0004)",
